  "raw": {
    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/AOQM/": {
      "title": "About the Opportunity",
      "description": "Manager, Academic Operations and Quality Back to Main Site Expression of Interest – Manager, Academic Operations and Quality About the Opportunity Alphacrucis University College is seeking expressions of interest from experienced higher education and VET professionals for the position of Manager, Academic Quality and Operations. This is a key role supporting the quality, governance and effective operational delivery of academic programs across Alphacrucis. The position is responsible for analysing and managing academic and administrative information, coordinating quality and governance activities, supporting course reviews and accreditation processes, and providing practical advice to academic and professional staff. Working closely with academic leaders, professional services teams and external stakeholders, the Manager will help ensure that academic operations and documentation align with regulatory requirements, institutional policies and quality standards. The role offers an opportunity for a highly organised and analytical professional to contribute to continuous improvement and the ongoing development of Alphacrucis' academic quality and governance framework. Key Responsibilities The Manager, Academic Quality and Operations will: Maintain and manage the institution's policy register, course register and VET scope, ensuring records accurately reflect review and accreditation activities. Maintain and monitor academic documentation, including subject outlines, course handbooks and student-facing information. Coordinate updates to website content relating to courses, subjects and policies to ensure information remains accurate and current. Administer student and lecturer surveys and collect, analyse and evaluate information to support institutional decision-making and reporting. Coordinate course reviews and course development projects, including timelines, resources, stakeholders, documentation and performance reporting. Analyse organisational processes, data and documentation to identify opportunities for improvement and recommend corrective or preventative actions. Support academic governance activities, including committee and subcommittee participation and preparation of governance reports, committee papers and supporting documentation. Provide advice to academic and professional staff on policy, procedures and organisational processes. Interpret regulatory requirements and translate them into practical operational guidance for internal stakeholders. Support the review and implementation of educational and administrative policies, procedures and systems. Monitor regulatory and sector developments, including TEQSA and ASQA requirements, and assess their operational impact. Coordinate third-party provider engagement, including relationship meetings, onboarding, compliance support and course delivery. Support registration and accreditation processes, including the preparation and coordination of applications and renewals with regulators and professional bodies. Coordinate process and system improvements across academic and administrative functions and monitor their effectiveness. Work collaboratively across departments and with external stakeholders to support high-quality course and project delivery. Undertake other duties consistent with the scope and objectives of the position. About You We are seeking a proactive, analytical and highly organised professional who can confidently work across academic quality, governance, compliance and operations. Qualifications and Experience You will have: A tertiary qualification in a relevant discipline. Previous experience in higher education and/or VET, particularly in a compliance, quality, policy or governance role. Demonstrated experience coordinating academic quality, governance, compliance or operational activities. Experience supporting course reviews, course development, accreditation, registration or regulatory processes. Experience managing academic documentation, policy registers, course information and institutional records. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify issues and recommend practical improvements. Experience providing policy, procedural or operational advice to academic and professional stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to manage projects, competing priorities and multiple stakeholders. Knowledge You will have knowledge of: The Higher Education Standards Framework (HESF). The VET Quality Framework. The ESOS Act and National Code. Higher education and VET quality and regulatory requirements. Academic governance and institutional policy frameworks. Records and information management, including document control, version control, privacy and retention obligations. Quality assurance and continuous improvement principles. Skills and Competencies The successful candidate will demonstrate: Attention to detail: Excellent attention to detail and strong written communication skills. Time management and organisation: Ability to deliver high-quality work within deadlines and manage competing priorities effectively. Information technology: Confidence and competence using IT applications, systems and databases. Teamwork: Ability to collaborate effectively with stakeholders across different teams and departments. Communication: Ability to communicate clearly and concisely and adapt communication style to different audiences. Commerciality: Ability to apply knowledge and regulatory requirements in a practical and outcomes-focused manner. Analytical skills: Ability to interpret data and information and use evidence to support recommendations and decision-making. Project coordination: Ability to coordinate projects, timelines, stakeholders and deliverables effectively. Personal Attributes You will bring: A professional and confident approach. Excellent organisational and time-management skills. Strong attention to detail. The ability to work effectively under pressure. A positive and adaptable approach to change. The ability to manage multiple concurrent tasks and competing priorities. Initiative and independent thinking, with sound judgement in resolving or escalating issues. A commitment to lifelong learning and ongoing professional development. Flexibility to respond to pressing deadlines and changing organisational priorities. A collaborative and solutions-focused approach. Committed to the Christian faith and aligned with AC’s mission and values. Why Join Alphacrucis? Alphacrucis University College is a Christian higher education provider committed to equipping students for lives of purpose, leadership and service. This role provides an opportunity to contribute to the quality and continuous improvement of academic programs while supporting effective governance, regulatory compliance and educational operations across the University College. Expression of Interest If you are an experienced higher education or VET professional with expertise in academic quality, governance, compliance or education operations, we invite you to submit an expression of interest. Please provide your CV and a brief statement outlining your relevant experience and suitability for the role to careers@ac.edu.au. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    },
    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/SCEM/": {
      "title": "About the Opportunity",
      "description": "Strategic Communications & Engagement Manager Back to Main Site Expression of Interest – Strategic Communications & Engagement Manager About the Opportunity Alphacrucis University College (AC) is seeking Expressions of Interest from an experienced and strategic communications professional to join the College as Strategic Communications & Engagement Manager and play a key role in strengthening AC’s public profile, reputation and engagement with key stakeholders and communities. Working within the President’s Office and closely with the National Director and Chief of Staff, the role will develop and deliver strategic communications, public relations, stakeholder engagement, events, digital content and public-facing initiatives that support AC’s strategic priorities. A key focus of the position will be the strategic development and operation of ACx, AC’s short-course and micro-credential platform. The role will oversee ACx’s communications, digital presence, customer experience, stakeholder engagement and external partnerships, helping position ACx as an accessible pathway for churches, schools, ministry organisations and other external audiences. Key Responsibilities Strategic Communications & Public Relations Develop, implement and evaluate strategic communications, public relations and engagement strategies that promote AC’s activities, offerings, public profile and community contribution. Advise senior leaders on communication and stakeholder considerations relating to organisational initiatives. Develop and oversee public-facing communications, publicity campaigns, digital content and other communications initiatives. Ensure communications align with AC’s brand, messaging, tone of voice and strategic priorities. Stakeholder Engagement Build and maintain strong relationships with churches, ACC, ministry organisations, professional networks, community partners and other key stakeholders. Represent AC at external functions, conferences, stakeholder meetings and other public-facing activities. Identify opportunities to strengthen AC’s community presence, relationships, reputation and public profile. Events & Public Engagement Lead the planning and delivery of College events, conferences, graduations, academic events and other public-facing initiatives. Develop event concepts, communication strategies and audience experiences that support organisational priorities. Coordinate internal teams, contractors, suppliers and external contributors to deliver successful events and engagement activities. ACx Development & External Engagement Lead the strategic development, operation and continuous improvement of ACx. Oversee the ACx digital ecosystem, including the LMS, website, web design, user experience, branding, digital workflows, social media and course presentation. Develop communications and engagement strategies to grow ACx’s reach and engagement. Manage ACx communications, customer support, stakeholder requirements and external partnerships. Monitor engagement and platform information to identify opportunities for growth and improvement. Content, Media & Communications Develop and oversee written, visual and audiovisual content promoting AC, its initiatives and educational offerings. Provide professional capability in videography, filming, video editing, colour grading and audiovisual post-production. Establish and maintain high-quality content and production standards consistent with AC’s brand and messaging. Strategic Advice & Functional Leadership Work closely with the National Director, Chief of Staff and senior stakeholders to identify communication, engagement and partnership opportunities. Provide specialist advice and subject matter expertise in communications, public relations, stakeholder engagement, events, ACx and digital media. Exercise professional autonomy in developing recommendations and translating organisational priorities into practical initiatives. Coordinate internal teams, contractors, suppliers and external stakeholders to achieve communication and engagement outcomes. About You You will be a confident communications and engagement professional who can combine strategic thinking with hands-on delivery. You will be comfortable working with senior leaders, managing multiple priorities and representing the College externally. Qualifications A Bachelor degree in Communications, Public Relations, Marketing, Media, Theology or a related discipline is desirable. Skills & Experience Experience in communications, public relations, stakeholder engagement, event coordination and/or digital content development. Experience working with senior leaders, external partners and community organisations. Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organisational, planning and problem-solving capabilities. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities and work independently. Experience developing and delivering communications and public-facing initiatives. Professional capability in digital content, videography and audiovisual production. Ability to coordinate events, campaigns, contractors, suppliers and external stakeholders. Strong understanding of strategic communications, public relations and audience engagement. Understanding of the Australian Christian Church landscape, particularly Pentecostal churches and the Pentecostal movement. An understanding of higher education and the mission of Christian education is desirable. Personal Attributes We are looking for someone who is: Professional, confident and adaptable. Strategic, proactive and solutions-focused. Highly organised and detail-oriented. An excellent relationship builder and communicator. Collaborative while also able to work autonomously. Able to exercise sound professional judgement. Committed to the Christian faith and aligned with AC’s mission and values. Why Join Alphacrucis? Alphacrucis University College is a Christian higher education provider committed to equipping students for lives of purpose, leadership and service. As Strategic Communications & Engagement Manager , you will have the opportunity to play a key role in shaping how AC communicates its mission, values and impact to the wider community. You will work closely with senior leadership to strengthen the College’s public profile, build meaningful stakeholder relationships and develop engaging communications, events and digital initiatives. Expression of Interest If you are an experienced communications, public relations, stakeholder engagement or digital media professional and are passionate about contributing to the mission and public profile of Alphacrucis University College, we invite you to submit an Expression of Interest for the Strategic Communications & Engagement Manager position. Please provide your CV and a brief statement outlining your relevant experience, key skills and suitability for the role to careers@ac.edu.au. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    },
    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/OMSE/": {
      "title": "About the Opportunity",
      "description": "Operations Manager, School of Education Back to Main Site Expression of Interest – Operations Manager, School of Education About the Opportunity Alphacrucis University College is seeking expressions of interest from experienced education professionals for the position of Operations Manager, School of Education . The Operations Manager provides strategic and operational support to the School of Education, ensuring effective systems, processes, resources and administrative arrangements are in place to support high-quality educational delivery. Working closely with the Head of School, Directors of Studies, academic staff and professional services teams, the role coordinates a broad range of school operations including academic planning, timetabling, student progression, teaching workforce coordination, accreditation and compliance, reporting, financial administration and continuous improvement. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced education operations or academic administration professional who enjoys working across multiple areas, solving complex operational issues and contributing to the effective delivery of tertiary education programs. Key Responsibilities The Operations Manager will: Plan, coordinate and review the School's educational and administrative operations across campuses and delivery modes. Coordinate annual and semester timetables, unit offerings and program delivery arrangements. Support academic planning through analysis of enrolment, progression and operational data. Coordinate student progression and educational administration processes and identify opportunities for improvement. Coordinate the planning and deployment of permanent and adjunct teaching staff, including workload, contracting and payment arrangements. Support accreditation, quality assurance, registration and regulatory reporting activities. Develop, implement and review operational policies, procedures, systems and controls. Prepare operational reports, recommendations and briefings for the Head of School and senior stakeholders. Monitor operational budgets and resources, including adjunct faculty payments and expenditure. Provide advice to academic and professional staff on operational and procedural matters. Liaise with internal directorates and external education stakeholders to resolve complex operational matters. Lead operational, accreditation and continuous-improvement projects within the School. Represent the School on relevant institutional committees and working groups. Contribute to institutional planning, governance and decision-making. About You We are seeking an organised, proactive and solutions-focused professional who can confidently coordinate complex education operations while building strong relationships with academic and professional staff. Essential Skills and Experience You will have: A bachelor's degree or higher qualification in education, educational administration, management, business administration or a relevant discipline. Substantial experience in education operations, academic administration or education management. Demonstrated experience coordinating educational and administrative operations within a tertiary education institution or comparable educational organisation. Experience in academic planning, timetabling, student progression, academic staffing and operational reporting. Experience coordinating accreditation, quality assurance or regulatory reporting processes. Experience developing and improving education administration systems, procedures and processes. Demonstrated ability to provide sound operational and procedural advice to senior academic and administrative stakeholders. Experience managing budgets, staffing arrangements or operational resources. Strong analytical, organisational and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Personal Attributes The successful candidate will demonstrate: Strong organisational and time-management skills. A professional, confident and collaborative approach. The ability to work effectively under pressure and manage competing priorities. Initiative and a willingness to identify and implement improvements. A positive and adaptable approach to change. The ability to build trust and positive working relationships. A willingness to learn and contribute to the broader life of the University. The ability to inspire and motivate others and contribute to long-term strategic goals. Commitment to Alphacrucis University College's Christian ethos, including being a practising Christian with active Church involvement. Additional Requirement Current NSW Working with Children Check (WWCC). Why Join Alphacrucis? Alphacrucis University College is a Christian higher education provider committed to equipping students for lives of purpose, leadership and service. This role provides an opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the operational success of the School of Education and to support the delivery of programs that prepare students for impact across education and the wider community. Expression of Interest If you are an experienced education operations or academic administration professional and are interested in contributing to the School of Education at Alphacrucis University College, we invite you to submit an expression of interest. Please provide your CV and a brief statement outlining your relevant experience and suitability for the role to careers@ac.edu.au. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    },
    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/PEASE/": {
      "title": "About the Role",
      "description": "Professional Experience Administrator - School of Education Back to Main Site Professional Experience Administrator - School of Education About the Role Alphacrucis University College (AC) is seeking a highly organised and service-focused Professional Experience Administrator to support the coordination and administration of professional experience placements across our education programs. The role is responsible for coordinating the administrative requirements of student placements in schools and early childhood centres, maintaining accurate placement records, supporting students and placement providers, and developing positive relationships with schools and centres. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced administrator who enjoys working with people, managing detailed information and contributing to the successful professional experience of future educators. Key Responsibilities In this role, you will: Source schools and early childhood centres for student placements through email and telephone communication. Establish and maintain positive, ongoing relationships with partner schools and centres. Coordinate and maintain accurate placement information in Sonia Online , including provider, student and placement records. Ensure placement details are accurate, including KLA/Stage, placement dates, mentors and Professional Experience Coordinators. Communicate placement information clearly to students, schools and early childhood centres to support successful placements. Monitor students’ mandatory placement requirements and documentation, escalating outstanding or non-compliant matters to the Director of Professional Experience. Provide day-to-day support to students undertaking professional experience, responding to enquiries and directing students to appropriate support. Liaise with the Director of Professional Experience regarding student placements and escalate issues or concerns as required. Maintain accurate records of placement-related communications and activities. Process and record payments to mentor teachers. Ensure administrative practices uphold the duty of care owed to children and reflect appropriate professional standards within school and early childhood settings. Undertake other placement-related administrative duties as required. About You You will be an organised, approachable and detail-oriented professional who enjoys providing high-quality administrative and customer service support. Essential Criteria Completion of a Certificate IV, Diploma or Bachelor’s degree from a recognised institution. Relevant and proven administrative experience. Experience maintaining databases and accurate records. Experience processing payments or financial administration. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent organisation and time management skills. A customer-service-focused approach and confidence communicating with a range of stakeholders. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team and independently manage competing priorities. A professional, courteous and positive approach to work. Commitment to the Christian faith, which informs professional and personal choices and commitments. Desirable Experience working in education, higher education, schools or early childhood settings. Experience using student placement, student management or database systems such as Sonia Online. Training will be provided, including role-specific systems and processes. Why Join AC? This is an opportunity to contribute to the development of future teachers and educators while working in a supportive university environment. You will play an important role in connecting students with schools and early childhood centres and helping ensure they have a positive and well-supported professional experience. How to Apply If you are an organised and people-focused administrator who enjoys building relationships and supporting students, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your CV and a brief cover letter outlining your relevant experience and suitability for the role via careers@ac.edu.au. Applications close: 15/09/2026 Note: only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    },
