    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/TSM/": {
      "title": "AC Tasmania State Manager",
      "description": "AC Tasmania State Manager Back to Main Site AC Tasmania State Manager About the Role The AC Tasmania State Manager plays a pivotal role in leading the day-to-day operations of AC’s Hobart Campus and creating an exceptional experience for students, staff, churches and other key stakeholders. Working as part of the State Directors Team, the Campus Manager will provide leadership across campus operations, student experience, staff coordination, community life, marketing and student recruitment. This is a dynamic, relationship-focused role suited to someone who is passionate about education, enjoys building relationships and is motivated to see students and the campus community thrive. The position is based primarily at our Hobart Campus, with the ideal working pattern being Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday on campus (7.35 hours per day), plus 4 hours on either Monday or Friday. What You’ll Be Responsible For Campus Operations Lead the day-to-day operations of the Hobart Campus, ensuring it runs effectively and provides a welcoming, professional and supportive environment. Coordinate local campus activities, facilities, communication and operational requirements. Identify operational needs and make sound, timely decisions to support the effective running of the campus. Community & Stakeholder Engagement Build and maintain strong relationships across Tasmania’s Christian community, including the Australian Christian Churches movement, local churches, schools, pastors and other organisations. Identify opportunities to strengthen AC’s presence and impact across Tasmania. Represent AC at relevant conferences, events and community initiatives. Student Experience & Support Support an exceptional student experience for Tasmanian students. Provide oversight of local pastoral care and academic support in partnership with the National Student Support team. Support student engagement strategies, including engagement in online environments. Contribute to initiatives that support student connection, engagement and retention. Student Recruitment & Growth Support student recruitment and enrolment activities for Tasmania. Coordinate prospective student enquiries and work with national Student Support and Marketing teams to grow local student numbers. Maintain awareness of Tasmanian enrolment, new student and retention targets and contribute to achieving these goals. Coordinate state-based marketing activities, including conferences, events and other initiatives that support enrolment and campus growth. Collaboration Work collaboratively with Student Services, Marketing, academic staff and the State Directors Team. Support effective communication, systems and student support across the campus and national teams. Contribute to a positive, collaborative and values-driven campus culture. About You We are looking for someone who is: Passionate about seeing people thrive and grow, with a genuine interest in education and student development. An exceptional communicator with strong emotional intelligence and interpersonal skills. A confident problem solver who can navigate challenging conversations with empathy and professionalism. Highly organised, proactive and able to work autonomously. Proficient with technology and able to learn and implement new systems. Flexible, positive and adaptable, with a willingness to think creatively and find solutions. A sound decision maker who can consider both operational requirements and the broader needs of the organisation. Confident and personable, with the ability to build strong relationships with a diverse range of people. Passionate about contributing to and engaging with the broader Christian community. Qualifications & Experience The successful candidate will ideally have: Strong administrative and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Demonstrated experience in customer service and stakeholder engagement. Experience working within or engaging with the broader Christian community. Experience in management, leadership or team coordination. Degree-level studies or equivalent relevant experience (desirable) . Knowledge of, or experience working within, the Australian tertiary education sector (desirable) . Why Join AC? At AC, you’ll be part of a purpose-driven organisation committed to developing people and making a positive impact through education. This is a great opportunity to step into a meaningful leadership role, support the Hobart Campus and its students, build strong connections across the Tasmanian Christian community and contribute to the growth of AC during a 12-month maternity cover period. Position Details Position: AC Tasmania State Manager Employment Type: Part-time, fixed-term maternity cover Contract Duration: 12 months Location: Hobart Campus, Tasmania Hours: 26.05 hours per week Ideal working pattern: Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday on campus (7.35 hours per day), plus 4 hours on either Monday or Friday Salary: $52,246.92 per annum, plus superannuation How to Apply If you are passionate about education, community and seeing people thrive, and you believe you can make a meaningful contribution to the AC across Tasmania, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your resume and a cover letter outlining your suitability for the role to careers@ac.edu.au. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    }
  },
